                {
                  "type": "quiz",
                  "question": "Why does Adler insist that the courage to be ordinary is the gateway to a peaceful life, not the sentence to a small one?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "text": "Because ordinary people have lower expectations and therefore experience less disappointment.",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Because being ordinary means dropping the demand to be above others, freeing you to find worth in contribution rather than superiority.",
                      "correct": true
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Because Adler believed achievement was morally wrong and that distinguishing yourself was selfish.",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Because ordinary people are better liked, which is the true measure of psychological health.",
                      "correct": false
                    }
                  ],
                  "explanation": "Ordinariness in Adler's sense is not low expectation — it is a *posture* that drops the vertical demand to be above. Once you stop needing to be above, contribution can carry your sense of worth, and contribution is sturdier than superiority. Option A makes ordinariness sound like apathy, which Adler explicitly rejects. Option C falsely moralizes — Adler did not condemn achievement; he condemned achievement-as-only-source-of-worth. Option D returns to vertical thinking (likeability as score) — exactly what Adler dismantles in Lesson 3.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Ordinariness as gateway, not sentence</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">THE GATEWAY</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"320\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Drop \"must be above\" →</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"360\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">contribution can carry worth.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"430\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">WHY STURDIER</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"535\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Superiority requires constant maintenance.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"570\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Usefulness is its own completion.</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"620\" width=\"700\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"675\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">WATCH THE TRAPS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"720\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">\"Lower expectations\" → apathy, not Adler</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"760\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">\"Achievement is wrong\" → false moralizing</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">\"Better liked\" → still vertical, just inverted</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"860\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Ordinary = posture, not result.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Releases you from the rung-race</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">while leaving excellence intact.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Posture releases. Excellence remains."
                  }
                }
