                  "explanation": "The move is the **proof of concept**, not the contradiction. Seneca's argument is that tranquility must be **internal first**. Once that is established, you are free to also choose a quieter environment — not because you depend on it, but because you have nothing to lose by it. The order matters: first internal work, then external choice. Seneca moves as a free man, not as a dependent one.",
